      "conclusion": "Lax48.ExponentialSeparation.exists_treewidth_le_and_two_pow_lt_twinWidth",
      "assumptions": [],
      "description": "Self-contained proof of the Bonnet–Déprés exponential gap: for every `k`, the\nBonnet–Déprés graph `BD_k` has treewidth at most `2*k + 4` while its\ntwin-width exceeds `2^k`.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Proof strategy",
          "markdown": "The source development phrases contraction sequences as trigraph state\nmachines; the proof bridges them to the submitted partition-based sequences\nthrough the invariant that black and red edges agree with completeness and\nnon-homogeneity in the graph, and relabels the result onto the canonical\nvertex type `Fin n`."
        },
        {
          "title": "Attribution",
          "markdown": "Ported from Édouard Bonnet's formalization of Bonnet–Déprés,\n*Twin-width can be exponential in treewidth* (JCTB 2023)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
